-- expect: a Semigroup instance targeting a literal record type (no alias
-- involved) is now accepted -- Eq/Ord/Show's own structural fallback was
-- never really the relevant distinction; this is exactly the case (an
-- interface with *no* structural fallback at all) a real user most wants
-- a custom instance for (corpus/programs/README.md's finding #5, widened
-- by `interfaces/vector2-custom-num.knot`'s own Num-on-a-record example).
-- Used to be InstanceTargetNotNominal before InstanceTable grew a second,
-- record-shaped key space alongside its Ref-keyed one.
instance Semigroup { x : Float } where
    (<>) a b =
        { x = a.x }
